// Lowering a value to the wire, for a card that cannot produce a compound one.
//
// Exactly one of `lower_scalar.wax` and `lower_values.wax` is concatenated, and
// which one decides what the module's IMPORT SECTION says. That is the point of
// the split: a host inspects imports to know what a guest can do, so a card
// with four scalar fields must not import the value arena merely because the
// generator can emit code that would use it. A capability not imported cannot
// be used, and asking for one is a promise rather than a grant.
//
// See `lower_values.wax` for the other half.

fn tc_lower(v: &jv_value, dest: i32) {
    if tc_lower_scalar(v, dest) == 1 { return; }
    // Unreachable in this build: a card that can hold a list is compiled with
    // `lower_values.wax` instead. Nil rather than a trap, because a wrong
    // answer the host can render beats taking the instance down.
    mem.store32(dest, tc_tag_nil);
    mem.store64(dest + 8, 0);
}

// A host may still hand IN a `%list` or a `%map` — as an event argument, say,
// from a view this card does not control. There is no arena import here to
// read it through, so it arrives as null. That is the same answer this card
// would give for any value it has no field to hold.
fn tc_lift_cell(p: i32) -> &jv_value {
    tc_lift_scalar_cell(p)
}
